From 2a4261703d276ef9c66697ffc5a73b9370ae8061 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:48:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 057/115] wifi: ath10k: bound the scan channel list to the size
 of the WMI array

struct wmi_start_scan_arg carries a fixed u16 channels[64], and
ath10k_hw_scan() copied cfg80211's whole list into it unchecked. Nothing
in cfg80211 caps a scan request at 64 channels -- it is bounded by the
number of non-disabled channels the wiphy advertises -- so a sufficiently
large regulatory domain, or a future band, walks off the end of an
on-stack structure.

No current ath10k device is known to hit it (the arg is built from the
driver's own channel tables, which stay under 64 today), so this is
hardening rather than a fix for an observed crash. Clamp and warn.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
index 154ac7a70982..4db75dc91eb7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -6463,7 +6463,17 @@ static int ath10k_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	}
 
 	if (req->n_channels) {
-		arg->n_channels = req->n_channels;
+		/*
+		 * arg->channels is a fixed 64-entry array and cfg80211 imposes
+		 * no such bound on a scan request, so clamp rather than run off
+		 * the end of it.
+		 */
+		arg->n_channels = min_t(u32, req->n_channels,
+					ARRAY_SIZE(arg->channels));
+		if (arg->n_channels != req->n_channels)
+			ath10k_warn(ar, "scan requested %d channels, truncating to %d\n",
+				    req->n_channels, arg->n_channels);
+
 		for (i = 0; i < arg->n_channels; i++)
 			arg->channels[i] = req->channels[i]->center_freq;
 	}
